JavaScript-only runtime patch. This directory must contain no native code,
codegen, native dependencies or config-plugin changes. Native patches stay in
the existing native fingerprint inputs; verify the official hash is unchanged
before publishing a JavaScript-only update. Do not edit native build records.

Legend List 3.7.0 (native): initial end placement can move short content above
its viewport when a row grows during bootstrap. The end target adds the row's
height delta to MVCP after the position adjustment, without clamping that final
delta to the available scroll range. React Native then applies that delta as a
native contentOffset change even after the list reports ready.

Clamp only active initial end-target adjustments to the physical scroll range.
Ordinary programmatic targets and the reader's existing anchors remain unchanged.
Both published native runtime entries are patched because this npm distribution
ships no source files. No generated native project/build output is included.

Remove when upstream bounds the final initial end-target MVCP adjustment after
both position and target-size changes. The core regression suite exercises the
actual installed CJS and ESM MVCP functions.

